==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_PermissionMatrix  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_PermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Clearing the permission matrix fact allows Alloy to assign any Role->OperationKind combination as Allowed, immediately violating LeastPrivilege (e.g. HospitalAdministrator -> RecordLookup becomes permitted). The injection forces exactly the violating cell to exist.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, PermissionCompleteness, PrivilegeMonotonicity, FR_017_AuditSearchAdminOnly, FR_018_AdminResponseContentBlind
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)
      - PermissionCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - PrivilegeMonotonicity: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_017_AuditSearchAdminOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_AdminResponseContentBlind: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_CareTeamGating  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_CareTeamGating.als
    rationale: Removing care-team gating allows a Permitted RecordLookup operation to exist for a clinician with no active CareTeamMembership, violating the core ownership-based access invariant. The injection forces such an operation into the model.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_004_CareTeamGating
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_004_CareTeamGating: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyNotes  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AppendOnlyNotes.als
    rationale: Removing the append-only note fact allows a ClinicalNote to exist that is not produced by any permitted AddNote operation, or allows two permitted AddNote operations to produce the same note object, violating the one-note-per-operation invariant.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_011_NotesAppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_011_NotesAppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Removing the audit-immutability fact allows an AuditEntry to exist that is not owned by any Operation, representing a spurious or orphaned audit record, which violates the bijection between Operations and AuditEntries that the AuditCompleteness assertion checks.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_014_AuditImmutability, AuditCompleteness
      - AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_014_AuditImmutability: PASS (vacuous?)
      - AuditCompleteness: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompleteness  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AuditCompleteness.als
    rationale: Clearing the audit-completeness fact allows two distinct Operations to share one AuditEntry, or an Operation to have no AuditEntry, directly contradicting the always-on one-to-one audit requirement from FR-012.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_012_AlwaysOnAudit
      - AuditCompleteness: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_012_AlwaysOnAudit: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AdminNotClinical  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AdminNotClinical.als
    rationale: Removing the administrator-cannot-access-clinical-content fact allows a HospitalAdministrator to have a Permitted RecordLookup operation, meaning the administrator could observe clinical content, violating the content-blindness invariants.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_005_AdminContentBlindness, FR_018_AdminResponseContentBlind, LeastPrivilege
      - NoInformationLeakage: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_005_AdminContentBlindness: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_018_AdminResponseContentBlind: PASS (vacuous?)
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)

